# Fixture for test_cif_reader_symmetry.cpp: a complete operator loop that
# is no tabulated setting: P 2 with the twofold axis along c through
# (1/4,0,z) instead of the origin, {x,y,z; -x+1/2,-y,z}. gemmi finds no
# table entry for these operators and expands the sites with the loop
# itself (UnitCell::images): Fe1 at (0.1,0.2,0.3) gives 2 atoms, the
# second at (0.4,-0.2,0.3). The record is reported as inconsistent ("space
# group from symops not found in the table", a WARNING).
data_P2_shifted_origin_loop
_cell_length_a 3.0
_cell_length_b 4.0
_cell_length_c 5.0
_cell_angle_alpha 90
_cell_angle_beta 90
_cell_angle_gamma 90
loop_
_symmetry_equiv_pos_as_xyz
'x,y,z'
'-x+1/2,-y,z'
loop_
_atom_site_label
_atom_site_type_symbol
_atom_site_fract_x
_atom_site_fract_y
_atom_site_fract_z
Fe1 Fe 0.1 0.2 0.3
